body:
Blocked by: #3, #15

### Context
PRD §29 (`init`), §4.1 (simple by default), §39 "Setup".

### Scope
- `init`:
  - detect `git`, `gh`, `tmux`, `claude`, `codex`;
  - ask which agent to use for implementer and reviewer, offering only installed ones;
  - ask for the first repository;
  - after confirmation, create missing labels (`ready-for-agent`, `agent-running`, `agent-needs-attention`) in it;
  - write the config;
  - run `doctor`.
- `repo add <owner/repo>`: validate access, append to config, offer to create labels.
- Both use the config writer from #3.

### Acceptance criteria
- On a machine with `git`, `gh`, `tmux`, and Claude Code installed and logged in, `mergeyard init` followed by `mergeyard` reaches a running dashboard watching one repository without hand-editing YAML (§39 "Setup").
- Re-running `init` with an existing config asks before overwriting.
